-- title:
--   Approximate identity of unit-factorizable test functions at principal level
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L$ a $K$-algebra, let $NK$ be an ideal of $\mathcal{O}_K$, and let $SK$ be a finite set of height-one primes of $\mathcal{O}_K$ containing every prime $p$ with $p \mid NK$. Let $tys$ be an archimedean type family for $L$, that is, a natural number $\mathrm{card}\,w$ for each infinite place $w$ of $L$ together with, for each $i < \mathrm{card}\,w$, a finite-dimensional complex representation of the group `rowIsometrySubgroup₀` of the completion at $w$. Let $f : \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L) \to \mathbb{C}$ be continuous, invariant under right translation by every element of $U := \mathrm{principalLevel}(\mathcal{O}_L, L, NK\,\mathcal{O}_L) \sqcap \mathrm{finiteAdelicGL2Subgroup}\,L$ — where the first factor is the intersection of `levelOne` at the ideal generated by the image of $NK$ with its conjugate by the Weyl element, and the second is the kernel of the archimedean-component homomorphism `glArch`, so that elements of $U$ have trivial archimedean part — and suppose $f$ lies in the archimedean cut $\bigsqcap_w \bigsqcup_{i} \mathrm{archTypeSubmoduleAt}\,L\,w\,(tys.\mathrm{rep}\,w\,i)$, the infimum over infinite places of the supremum of the type submodules cut out by the listed representations via `rowIsometryInclAt₀`. Then there is a sequence $\varphi : \mathbb{N} \to (\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L) \to \mathbb{C})$ such that each $\varphi_n$ is unit-factorizable above $K$ of type $tys$ for the level $U$ and the set $SK$, i.e. $\varphi_n$ is bi-invariant under $U$, admits a semi-local factorization over $K$, $L$, $SK$ into archimedean, finite and $SK$-parts, and is archimedean bi-finite for $tys$ (both $g \mapsto \varphi_n(g^{-1})$ lies in the archimedean cut and $\varphi_n$ lies in the dual archimedean cut); and for every $g$ the convolutions $\int f(gx)\,\varphi_n(x)\,dx$, taken against the adelic Haar measure on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$, converge to $f(g)$ as $n \to \infty$.
--
--   This is the construction of an approximate identity on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ by test functions of controlled shape: invariant on both sides under a principal congruence level with trivial archimedean part, factorizable semi-locally over the finite places above $K$, and of prescribed finite archimedean type. It is used in the proof that the isotypic cuspidal submodule at principal level, intersected with the archimedean cut, is finite-dimensional.
